\f0\b\fs32 \cf2 \cb3 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Shenmen HE-7 (Spirit Gate)
\f1\b0 \'a0is the foremost acupuncture point on the body to calm and regulate the spirit. It is classically indicated for insomnia, frequent talking during sleep, poor memory, and anxiety. Whether the spirit is disrupted by deficiency (malnourishment of Heart blood or yin) or excess (Heart fire, phlegm, or phlegm-fire), Shenmen HE-7 acts as the anchor point to restore peace and quiet the mind.\cb1 \

\f0\b \cb3 Sanyinjiao SP-6 (Three Yin Intersection)
\f1\b0 \'a0is classically included in a vast array of prescriptions for any kind of insomnia, usually in direct combination with\'a0
\f0\b Shenmen HE-7
\f1\b0 . Because it tonifies qi and blood, nourishes Liver and Kidney yin, spreads Liver qi, and harmonizes the digestion, SP-6 addresses the physiological root of multiple sleep patterns.\cb1 \

\f0\b \cb3 Anmian (N-HN-54 / M-HN-34, Peaceful Sleep)
\f1\b0 \'a0is an extraordinary point located behind the ear that is specifically celebrated in modern practice for the direct treatment of insomnia, alongside agitation, restlessness, and palpitations.\cb1 \

\f0\b \cb3 Yintang (M-HN-3, Hall of Impression)
\f1\b0 \'a0is a prominent extraordinary point at the glabella utilized as a powerful tool to calm the spirit for insomnia, anxiety, and general agitation. Classically, a highly effective combination pairing\'a0
\f0\b Yintang (M-HN-3)
\f1\b0 ,\'a0
\f0\b Shenmen HE-7
\f1\b0 , and\'a0
\f0\b Sanyinjiao SP-6
\f1\b0 \'a0is used to resolve insomnia.\cb1 \

\f0\b \cb3 Yongquan KID-1 (Gushing Spring)
\f1\b0 \'a0is the lowest channel point on the body and is highly effective at clearing excess from the head. Clinically, it is used to treat insomnia by strongly drawing pathologically ascending yang, Liver fire, or qi downwards. Massaging Yongquan KID-1 before sleep or soaking the feet in hot water is a traditional practice to anchor this excess yang and induce sleep.\cb1 \

\f0\b \cb3 Neiguan P-6 (Inner Pass)
\f1\b0 \'a0is a major point for regulating and calming the spirit, making it a primary selection to treat insomnia, poor memory, and apprehension.\cb1 \

\f0\b \cb3 Shenmai BL-62 (Extending Vessel)
\f1\b0 \'a0is classically selected for insomnia caused by defensive qi remaining in the yang channels, which results in "excessive opening of the eyes" and an inability to close them. It is often paired with its coupled vessel point,\'a0
\f0\b Zhaohai KID-6
\f1\b0 , to balance yin and yang and regulate sleep.\cb1 \
